  "query_preview": "..Satellite imagery this morning showed partly to \nmostly cloudy conditions associated with short-wave trof moving \nacross the state. A few light snow or mixed rain & snow possible\nthrough 8 am for far northern Greenlee county. Otherwise the \nclouds will push on east through mid-afternoon followed by \nincreasing high clouds from late this afternoon into tonight. \nCooler air mass settles in overnight that may result in near \nfreezing low temperatures Sunday morning across some of the \neastern valleys. Although the high cloud cover may limit \ntemperatures reaching the forecast lows, I went ahead and \nupgraded the freeze watch to warning.\n\nProgressive weather pattern continues with a couple more dry\ntrof moving through, one on Monday and the other on Wednesday to\nearly Thursday. Ridging aloft moves into the desert SW Friday\nand Saturday. The following week will see the progressive \nweather pattern continuing but with the storm track further \nsouth with the potential for increased precipitation chances to \nstart December.\n\n8-14 day outlooks (Sat Nov 28 to Fri Dec 4)\nTemperature: Leaning above normal (39%-47%)\nPrecipitation: Slightly above normal (34%-37%)",
